hinder|PASS: Traffic delaying shelves illustrates obstruction without falsely requiring a complete stop, improving the source's overly absolute wording. Vietnamese cản trở and delivery object are accurate. Hinder progress/from doing valency is sound.
impression|PASS: Effect made by a restored hall and uncertain belief about meeting timing are separate source-supported noun boundaries. Vietnamese distinguishes ấn tượng from có cảm giác. Make an impression on and have the impression that match the examples; neither proposal asserts the belief is fact.
peel|PASS: Carrot skin removal fits gọt vỏ, followed faithfully by thin-strip cutting. Transitive peel and regular forms are accurate. The grammatical contrast does not allocate an unsupported noun or figurative boundary.
surprising|PASS: Unexpected variety of birds fits a cause-of-surprise adjective, with Vietnamese preserving colourful birds rather than changing the garden itself. Surprising versus surprised is useful; no arbitrary species count or scientific fact is asserted.
wait|PASS: Waiting for a guide and a ferry-wait period illustrate verb and countable noun separately. Vietnamese retains beside the ticket office and nearly an hour. For/to complements and exclusion of separate wait-on meanings are accurate.
